<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Axiom Power Services provides <strong>rotating equipment services in Nigeria</strong> for plants that cannot absorb unplanned stoppages. We work on centrifugal and reciprocating compressors, single and multistage pumps, fans, blowers, gearboxes and their drive trains, from routine condition monitoring through to full strip, inspect and rebuild. Our engineers are based in Lagos and mobilise to sites in Rivers, FCT, Kaduna, Delta and Kano States.</p><p>The work is diagnostic before it is mechanical. We take vibration spectra, phase readings, alignment measurements and process data first, then tell you which machines on your list actually need to be opened during the outage. That keeps the outage window short and keeps spend on the assets that are genuinely degrading rather than on the whole population. Where a critical spare is obsolete or the import lead time is unacceptable, we reverse engineer the part and manufacture it locally.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Handle</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">What's Included in Every Visit</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Centrifugal and Reciprocating Compressors</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Air, nitrogen and process gas machines: valve and unloader work, piston, ring and rod replacement, cylinder honing, impeller and diaphragm inspection and full running clearance checks. We record as found and as left clearances against OEM limits so your asset file carries a real baseline.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Industrial Pumps</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Overhung, between bearings and vertical turbine pumps on boiler feed, fuel transfer, water treatment and process duty. We address seal leakage, cavitation damage, wear ring clearance loss and shaft deflection instead of swapping the pump and repeating the failure.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Fans, Blowers and Air Handling</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">ID and FD fans, roots blowers and cooling tower fans, including in situ balancing of rotors that cannot be sent off site. Blade erosion, fouling and bearing housing looseness are the failure modes we see most often on Nigerian plants.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Vibration Analysis and Condition Monitoring</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Route based data collection with spectrum, time waveform and phase analysis to separate unbalance, misalignment, looseness, bearing defects and blade pass problems. Findings are reported against ISO 20816 severity zones with a recommended action date, not a vague warning.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Laser Alignment and Dynamic Balancing</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Laser shaft alignment of motor, gearbox and driven machine trains, with soft foot corrected and thermal growth targets applied before final readings. Field balancing of fans and rotors to ISO 21940 grades using a portable analyser, with residual unbalance recorded.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Reverse Engineering and Local Spares Manufacture</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Dimensional capture, material verification and local machining of impellers, shafts, sleeves, wear rings, coupling spacers and gland components. This removes the 10 to 20 week import lead time and the FX exposure that sits inside it.</p>
      </div>
</div>
